---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PolicyNote from '../components/PolicyNote.astro';
import policies from '../data/policy-updates.json';
import '../styles/learning.css';
---
<Base title="What's changed in Australian money rules?" description="Understand changes to Australian home-buyer support, property tax and foreign-buyer rules. See who is affected, when changes apply and the official sources.">
<header class="hl-page-head hl-wrap lesson-header"><div class="hl-breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a> / Rule updates</div><h1>What's changed?</h1><p>The change. Who it affects. What to check next.</p></header>
<div class="hl-wrap lesson-shell"><p class="hl-help">A proposal is not a law. A passed law may start later. Status is based on the dated source check, not a live legal service.</p>
{policies.map(p=><PolicyNote id={p.id} full/>)}
<details class="lesson-more"><summary>Site updates & corrections</summary><p><strong>18 September 2026 — usability and content review:</strong> Expanded all eight shorter money lessons with worked examples. Improved amount formatting and total mortgage-payment labels; added explicit base-versus-conditional bank scenarios with welcome-period expiry. Tax preparation now supports optional saving, restoring and clearing on this device. Aligned page addresses and sitemaps, and updated the privacy notice to describe the deployed Cloudflare traffic beacon.</p><p><strong>18 September 2026:</strong> Added eight beginner lessons, an LVR calculator, source-review dates and a rule-change record. Lessons start with an example and a quick check; detailed explanations remain available below.</p><div class="hl-content"><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Employee tax return companion</h2><p>Added a <a href="/tax-return">three-step preparation guide</a> with income-year and coverage checks, occupation sources, record reminders, six expense topics, a local expense organiser and downloadable CSV and myTax checklists. Expense arithmetic separates private use and work-use reimbursements; it does not assess tax deductibility. It does not decide deductions, estimate refunds or lodge returns. The guided flow runs without AI; optional AI explanations are disabled until separately configured.</p></section><section><h2><time datetime="2026-09-18">18 September 2026</time> — Australian money tools</h2><ul><li>Introduced compound-interest, mortgage and offset, savings-goal and emergency-fund calculators with assumptions and calculation breakdowns.</li><li>Published the bank explorer with dated public CDR product snapshots. Missing or partial data is labelled. Supported base rates are modelled separately from bonus and introductory components.</li><li>Expanded six money guides with worked comparisons, common mistakes and primary-source references.</li><li>Added a starting-point guide, topic navigation and individual article update records.</li><li>Separated older everyday how-to guides into a labelled archive. Their existing URLs remain available; they are outside the current money-guide library.</li></ul><p><a href="/methodology">Calculation and data methods →</a></p></section><section><h2>How a correction is handled</h2><p>Send the page URL, the part that seems wrong and a source or reproducible example to the address on our <a href="/contact">contact page</a>. Use sample amounts and leave out account identifiers.</p><p>A verified error in a formula, example or explanation is corrected in the affected page. A material change should be recorded here or in the article's update note. Typographical or layout changes do not need to be presented as a new factual review.</p></section><section><h2>What an update date means</h2><p>A guide's publication date records when it first appeared. Its update date records a material edit; a source-check date records a check of its cited references. Bank retrieval dates describe a separate data snapshot and cannot guarantee a current offer. None of these dates means a licensed adviser has reviewed the page.</p></section><p><a href="/editorial-policy">Read the publishing policy →</a></p></div></details>
</div></Base>